<title>MEXICO: RESEARCH ALERT-Moderna downgraded to hold.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Moderna downgraded to hold.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Flemings Research said on Wednesday it had downgraded Mexican conglomerate Empresas la Moderna to hold from long-term buy due to &quot;weaker than expected&quot; first quarter 1997 earnings.</p>
<p>-- Analyst Terry Sigler wrote in a research report that Moderna's first quarter earnings showed &quot;a deterioration in cigarette volumes and less optimistic growth forecast for seeds.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Sigler revised full-year 1997 earnings estimates down to 2.09 pesos per share from 2.17 pesos.</p>
<p>(( --Martin Roberts, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7907))</p>
